// Deviates from the sheet's own `Explosion` variant for the same reason
// shatter.ron in this folder documents (and acid_splash.ron before it):
// `CharacterAbility::Explosion` always detonates centered on the caster,
// with no target-point field, so it cannot express "a bead of flame
// streaks to a point [up to 45 m away]". Uses `GroundAoe` instead --
// dark_star.ron (Axiomancy, circle 9) is the sibling shape this was cloned
// from, the same precedent acid_splash.ron/shatter.ron already establish.
//
// `GroundAoe` hardcodes `DamageKind::Energy`
// (common/src/states/ground_aoe.rs) -- despite the Fire flavor text this
// deals generic Energy damage under the hood, same drift acid_splash.ron/
// shatter.ron document.
//
// The sheet notes call this "the archetypal scalable burst -- circle 3,
// scales up cleanly." Calibrated against the closest same-circle sibling,
// gory_eruption.ron (Hemomancy, `Explosion`, circle 3: damage 50, energy
// 98, radius 4) -- damage/energy set slightly below it (48/90) to account
// for `GroundAoe`'s ranged safety (cast from up to 45 m away, vs.
// `Explosion`'s self-centered melee-range risk), and radius scaled up to
// match the sheet's own Sphere r6 (vs. gory_eruption's r4). Flagged for
// wave-close-out balance review.
GroundAoe(
    energy_cost: 90.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    delay: 0.35,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    max_range: 45.0,
    radius: 6.0,
    min_falloff: 0.3,
    damage: 48,
    poise: 20,
    knockback: (strength: 12, direction: Away),
    dodgeable: Roll,
    rooted_cast: false,
    meta: (school: Some(Evocation), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
